About the Role:
We are looking for a proactive and detail-oriented General QA Engineer who can own the full testing lifecycle. This role is ideal for a strong junior or mid-level specialist who is comfortable working independently, collaborating with developers and product teams, and ensuring high product quality from requirements to release.
Responsibilities:
Perform full-cycle testing: from requirements analysis to release validation;
Design, write, and maintain test documentation (test cases, checklists, test plans);
Conduct manual testing of web and/or mobile applications;
Identify, document, and track bugs (e.g., using Jira or similar tools);
Perform regression, smoke, sanity, and exploratory testing;
Collaborate closely with developers, product managers, and designers;
Participate in grooming, planning, and sprint activities;
Validate requirements and provide early feedback on potential issues;
Support release processes and post-release verification.
Requirements:
4+ years of professional experience in QA
Commercial experience with Playwright + TS
Understanding of QA methodologies, testing types, and software development lifecycle (SDLC);
Experience with manual testing of web applications (mobile is a plus);
Ability to write clear and structured test documentation;
Experience with bug tracking systems (e.g., Jira, YouTrack, etc.);
Basic knowledge of API testing (Postman, Swagger, etc.);
Understanding of client-server architecture;
Basic SQL knowledge for data validation;
Experience working in Agile/Scrum teams;
Good analytical thinking and attention to detail;
English level: Intermediate or higher (written and spoken).

Project Overview
We are looking for a Junior Manual QA Engineer to join Group107 for a WordPress department. The main focus of this role is design-oriented QA — verifying that developed websites and digital products accurately reflect approved designs, are pixel-perfect, responsive, and visually consistent across all devices. The role starts with WordPress projects and expands over time to cover broader web QA tasks.

Requirements
Strong attention to detail and a sharp visual eye for noticing small design differences;
Good knowledge of responsive web layouts and ability to identify inconsistencies across breakpoints;
Ability to compare developed pages against Figma/design files and document mismatches precisely;
Basic understanding of WordPress and willingness to learn quickly;
Ability to write clear, structured bug reports understandable by both developers and designers;
Upper-intermediate+ level of English;
Highly detail-oriented, patient, and organized in day-to-day work;
Team player with clear communication skills when working with developers, designers, and project managers;
Self-motivated with a willingness to learn new tools and QA practices quickly.

Nice to Have
Hands-on experience with WordPress (admin panel, page editing);
Experience working with Figma (reviewing designs, using inspect mode);
Basic HTML/CSS understanding — enough to identify layout and styling root causes;
Experience with Jira, ClickUp, Trello, or similar task management tools;
Familiarity with Gutenberg blocks;
Basic accessibility awareness;
Experience testing multilingual websites.

Responsibilities
Compare developed pages against approved Figma/design files and report visual discrepancies (spacing, alignment, typography, colors, icons, images) clearly and accurately;
Test WordPress pages after development — checking Gutenberg/custom blocks from both the user side and admin side, verifying menus, headers, footers, forms, buttons, and page sections;
Test responsive behavior across desktop, tablet, and mobile; flag layout breaks and inconsistencies;
Perform pre-delivery checks before client review, ensuring the final result matches the approved design;
Write structured, clear bug reports and communicate findings to developers and designers;
Over time, support additional manual QA tasks — functional testing, cross-browser testing, regression testing after bug fixes, and checklist-based acceptance verification.

Growth Potential
This role is designed for someone who grows over time. Expected progression includes:

Full manual QA ownership for WordPress projects
QA coverage for broader web platforms and landing pages
Creating and maintaining test cases and QA checklists
Regression testing and release QA ownership
Accessibility QA basics
Future automation QA basics, if relevant

